{title: Lanterns on the Water}
{artist: The Quiet Harbour}
{key: G}
{capo: 2}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Lanterns on the [Em]water, drifting [C]out to the [D]bay
[G]Every little [Em]light is a [C]word we didn't [D]say
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
So [C]let them go, let them [G]glow
Down the [D]river where the [Em]cold winds blow
[C]Hold me close till the [D]morning [G]comes
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Paper boats and [Em]promises, [C]folded by the [D]shore
[G]One for every [Em]summer that we [C]won't see any[D]more
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Am]Tide comes in, [C]tide goes out
[Em]Nothing stays but the [D]sound
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus: Final Chorus}
